{
    "background_story": "Eliseo was a young anthropologist who had always been fascinated by the diverse cultures of China. During his research, he stumbled upon the Bouyei people, an ethnic minority group living in the mountains of Guizhou Province. Eliseo was captivated by their rich traditions and customs, and he decided to dedicate his life to studying and preserving their unique heritage. He spent years living among the Bouyei, learning their language, and participating in their festivals. Eliseo's respect and admiration for the Bouyei culture earned him the title of 'honorary son' among the community. He worked tirelessly to document and promote their history, arts, and traditions, ensuring that the Bouyei people's legacy would be cherished for generations to come. Eliseo's love and dedication to the Bouyei culture had a profound impact on the community, and he remained a cherished friend and advocate for the rest of his life.",
